{"kind": "report", "step": 15, "ts": "2026-11-19T15:43:06.354893+00:00", "data": {"category": "wan", "host": "gw.lan", "component": "wan_dhcp_lease", "cause": "The ISP-side session was reset when the cable modem lost sync and self-rebooted (~02:01\u201302:28), but the firewall's WAN interface still carries the old lease (198.51.100.27, renew not due until 2026/3/5), so its address is no longer valid on the provider side and traffic to the gateway 198.51.100.1 is dropped; the WAN watchdog only recorded this in observe mode and never actually reloaded the interface.", "evidence": ["/var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-events.jsonl: 'No Ranging Response received - T3 time-out' at 02:01:44, 'TFTP failed - configuration file NOT FOUND' at 02:14:10, then 'Cable Modem Reboot ... registration complete' at 02:28:21 \u2014 outage began with a modem sync loss and reboot.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/modem-metrics.jsonl: cm_status NOT_SYNCHRONIZED at 02:06, OPERATIONAL from 02:29 onward \u2014 the modem itself is healthy and registered again now.", "/var/db/wan-watchdog/events.jsonl + state.json: decisions 'none' while modem was down/settling, then 'reload'/'would_reload' at 02:30 and 02:40 in mode 'observe' \u2014 the intended WAN reload was never applied (reloads_in_outage counted but mode is observe).", "ifconfig vtnet0: still UP with inet 198.51.100.27, link active \u2014 interface itself is fine.", "cat /var/db/dhclient.leases.vtnet0: lease for 198.51.100.27 with renew scheduled 2026/3/5 \u2014 nothing triggered a renew after the 02:28 re-registration, so the address is stale relative to the provider.", "ping -c 3 198.51.100.1: 100% packet loss to the ISP gateway while local routing table still defaults via it \u2014 consistent with the provider no longer recognizing the old lease."], "action": "change_config", "recommendation": "Reconfigure the WAN interface on gw.lan to renew the DHCP lease (wan_reload), which should pick up a fresh address from the provider now that the modem is registered again. Afterwards, consider moving the WAN watchdog out of observe mode so it can act on its own 'reload' decisions.", "detail": "WAN holds a stale pre-reboot DHCP lease; never renewed after the modem re-registered", "fix": "wan_reload", "contributing": {"host": "gw.lan", "component": "modem"}}}
